# Patch series for MT6765V (Helio G99) -- EXPERIMENTAL / UNVERIFIED
#
# Nothing here has been built, booted or measured. See
# patches/0000-MT6765V-experimental-perf-cover.txt for the honesty statement
# and for the list of forbidden changes (thermal / lmk / max clocks) that are
# deliberately absent.
#
# Base tree : https://github.com/oppo-source/android_kernel_oppo_mt6765
# Branch    : oppo/mt6765_u_14.0_oppo_a77
# Commit    : 9b1c9a531dd08e68bf778dcf7ed13f811ec1f153  (Linux 4.19.191)
# Base cfg  : arch/arm64/configs/k65v1_64_bsp_defconfig  (CONFIG_MACH_MT6765=y)
#
# Ordering is by RISK, ascending. Bring up the cheap ones first so that a
# measurement failure in P05 is never confused with a regression elsewhere.

# --- low risk, independent, start here ---------------------------------------
01-io-sched-deadline.config            # I/O      CFQ -> deadline
02-mem-nr-cpus-8.config                # Memory   NR_CPUS 64 -> 8
03-sched-no-autogroup.config           # Sched    drop SCHED_AUTOGROUP
04-cpufreq-governors-minimal.config    # Power    drop powersave+conservative governors

# --- gated: run the grep in the header BEFORE applying ------------------------
06-sched-no-mtk-sched-tracers.config   # Sched    drop MTK sched tracers [GATED]

# --- high risk, LAST and ALONE: expect vendor-module link failures ------------
05-lto-thin.config                     # Build    enable ThinLTO [HIGH RISK]
